{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nS1-S6 provide the new composition paths, but RP-04 is not complete while legacy ambient reads can return or future code can bypass the central seam. The recovered design explicitly requires an AST ownership guard, generated operator documentation, hosted parity/delta canaries, and contract-phase removal. The existing `scripts/check_config_reads.py` proves each schema field is consumed; it does not prove only approved owners consume configuration.\n\n## Outcome\nEnforce centralized ownership with a separate deterministic AST gate, wire it into the portable local gate and CI, generate configuration/security lifecycle documentation from the authoritative registry, run final canaries, and remove legacy facades only after all proof passes.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and an explicit registry of approved composition roots/provider boundaries. Reject direct/aliased `load_config`, `os.getenv`, `os.environ.get`, `os.environ[...]`, backend property reload, known credential reads, and configurable adapter defaults below those seams. Test-only controls and protocol constants require exact path+symbol+rationale entries, not broad path globs.\n2. Add synthetic red-proof fixtures for every prohibited syntax/alias and self-tests that deliberately insert a new bypass. The gate reports path, symbol, access kind, and owning seam. Legacy migration exceptions are exact, shrink-only, and empty before close.\n3. Wire the guard through `make lint` (portable/no-CI path) and the build workflow; extend CI parity tests so the workflow cannot silently omit it. Keep `check_config_reads.py` as the opposite-direction field-consumption gate.\n4. Generate the config precedence/source/lifecycle reference in `docs/config.md` and a new indexed `docs/security.md` from schema plus ownership/secret-name registries; update `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation. Drift checks cover MCP/CLI exposure, restart/redeploy rotation, native refresh, observability exception, subprocess limitations, and explicit behavior deltas.\n5. Run focused suites and bounded Anthropic/Bedrock, AWS review-bot/op-cert, reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries. Compare redacted snapshot fingerprints and provider-neutral outcomes; record each approved delta. Then delete legacy ambient/per-job facades, migration switches, and exception entries.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Structural change-detector tests feed synthetic modules for direct and aliased imports/calls, each environment access shape, backend property reload, credential-name access, configurable duplicate default, broad/glob exception, missing rationale, and expired migration exception; each must fail with the expected diagnostic.\n- Real-tree held-out tests assert the ownership registry maps each approved read to one seam, the legacy exception set is empty, generated docs are current, and local/CI invocation exists.\n- Behavioral regression suites from S1-S6 remain the correctness oracle; the AST gate supplements rather than substitutes for them.\n- [operator-attested] Live evidence includes run/change ids, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry/cache counters where applicable, redacted fingerprint/outcome, and rollback decision. No credential value/path is recorded.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDo not remove a legacy facade until its focused suite and bounded live path pass. Before removal, rollback selects the facade. At contract phase, retain only the S1 snapshot-envelope compatibility floor; rollback below it is unsupported and documented. Stored ticket/event/bridge/binding formats remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every synthetic prohibited access/alias/default/exception fixture fails the ownership gate with path, symbol, access kind, and expected owning seam; clean approved fixtures pass.\n- [ ] `make lint` and CI execute both ownership-direction and existing field-consumption gates, and parity tests fail if either invocation disappears.\n- [ ] The real tree has no direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable adapter default below approved seams; the legacy exception set is empty and no exception uses a path glob.\n- [ ] Generated config/security/operator docs are byte-current with schema/ownership registries and cover every lifecycle, precedence, restart, observability, subprocess, and behavior-delta topic named in the epic.\n- [ ] All S1-S6 behavioral suites pass after legacy removal; structural gates remain change detectors, not substitutes for those observable oracles.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Bounded provider, AWS review-bot/op-cert, and reconciler check/dry-run/live canaries pass with required redacted evidence and no unauthorized fallback/leakage.\n- [ ] Legacy facades, switches, per-job SSM path, ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their proof passes; documented rollback retains the snapshot-envelope compatibility floor."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786995749743124001,"uuid":"25df45bc-0a6c-4483-b059-6a0e58dcc9bd"}